<title>USA: Digital eyes manufacturing consolidation-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Digital eyes manufacturing consolidation-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp is considering consolidating its manufacturing facilities, after announcing a reorganization of its sales and marketing operations, the Wall Street Journal said in Thursday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Company insiders said a manufacturing consolidation was part of the reason behind the sales and marketing consolidation, the paper said.</p>
<p>Digital Chief Executive Robert Palmer said he had not yet decided about manufacturing operations, according to the paper.</p>
<p>But people familiar with his thinking expect the company to announce a consolidation of the personal computer and computer server and workstation manufacturing in coming months, if not sooner, the paper said.</p>
<p>((New Nork newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
